# title variant=film place=village text="WHY IS VIETNAM|AN S?" sub="Ep. 3" trans=fgwipe
Why is Vietnam an S?

# sshape mode=terrain stages="938;Independence" sfx="0.4:rumble:0.4|2.2:tape_rewind:0.3"
Year 938. Đại Việt wins its independence, up north.
China above. Mountains to the west. Sea to the east.
And rice needs flat, wet land.
That flat land runs one way: south, down the coast.

# sshape mode=grow face=yes trans=lightleak stages="938;|1069;A war with Champa|1306;A royal wedding"
Only problem? The coast already had owners: the kingdom of *Champa*.
1069. After a war, the border moves south.
1306. The most expensive wedding gift in history.

# moment kind=split a=court b=champa labels="ĐẠI VIỆT|CHAMPA" heroA=anhtong heroB=cheman timeA=day timeB=sunset
Two kings. One deal.

# dialogue a=cheman b=anhtong place=court voiceA=bm_george voiceB=am_fenrir lines="a:neutral:I'd like to marry Princess Huyền Trân.|b:thinking:And the gift?|a:smug:Two provinces.|b:joy:…Deal."

# sshape mode=grow face=yes stages="1306;Ô & Lý → Huế|1471;Vijaya falls|1653;Settlers move south"
Those two provinces? Today, that's around Huế.
1471. Champa's capital falls. This part was not a wedding.
Then, generation after generation, farmers keep moving south.

# gag place=sidewalk hero=dave mood=happy react=shocked reactPose=scared punch="AGAIN?!" cam=snap capY=.44
And in 1620… another royal marriage. With Cambodia.

# sshape mode=grow face=yes stages="1653;|1698;Prey Nokor → Sài Gòn|1757;The Mekong Delta|today;"
A Khmer fishing village called Prey Nokor…
…becomes Sài Gòn, in 1698.
1757. The Mekong Delta. The S is complete.
Seven hundred years. One very long coastline.

# talk place=towers host=cham mood=happy pose=present act="cham:present" shots="WS cham|MS cham|CU cham" cam=crane fg=leaves
But Champa didn't vanish.
Its towers still stand: Mỹ Sơn, near Hội An, and Po Nagar, in Nha Trang.
And Cham families still live along this coast.

# dialogue a=copho b=dave place=sidewalk voiceA=af_bella voiceB=am_puck lines="a:smug:Guess how wide it is at the waist.|b:thinking:Five hundred kilometres?|a:laugh:Fifty."

# sshape mode=narrow label="≈ 50 KM" sub="at the waist, near Đồng Hới"
At its narrowest, Vietnam is about fifty kilometres wide.

# sshape mode=length trans=burn label="1,650 KM" sub="≈ 34 h by train"
And top to bottom? One thousand six hundred and fifty kilometres.
Hà Nội to Sài Gòn by train: about thirty-four hours.

